alue of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of yellow white fibroadipose breast tissue  which is submitted entirely as FX 1 and resubmitted as Cassette A  Also received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number  and  left adjacent  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fibroadipose breast tissue with a tan stellate mass with fibrous extension  which is submitted entirely in Cassettes B E  Also received   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy cavity   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose breast tissue  with suture marking edge farthest from the tumor  The specimen is inked black and the edge farthest from the tumor is over inked blue  The entire specimen is submitted in Cassettes F I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  submitted entirely in Cassettes J K  Resident  SAMANTHA J  PULLIAM  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  Dr  Prabha Pai O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                               