en is inked as follows  medial in red  lateral in yellow  anterior in blue  posterior  with double stitch  in black  Sectioning the specimen from medial to lateral reveals the tan white firm area appreciated from the external surface  which abuts all margins  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette L S  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan green lymph node with attached fibroadipose tissue  which is bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette T  Resident  Mari Mino  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL    report_end  , 0.
